00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.620
In this episode, we'll be
talking about Google Compute

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:16.450
Engine.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.920
Google Compute Engine
delivers virtual machines

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.840
running in Google's
innovative data centers

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.820
and worldwide fiber network.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.010
Compute Engine's tooling
and workflow support

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:28.460
enables scaling from instances
to global load balanced cloud

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.450
computing.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.730
Compute Engine's
VMs boot quickly,

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:33.560
come with persistent
disk storage,

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.840
and deliver consistent
performance.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.460
Our virtual servers
are available

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.790
in many configurations,
including predefined sizes

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:44.030
or the option to create
custom machine types optimized

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.530
for your specific needs.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.156
In this hands-on
lab, you'll learn

00:00:47.156 --> 00:00:49.530
how to launch a Windows Server
instance on Google Compute

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:53.570
Engine and connect to it using
the remote desktop protocol.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.020
If you aren't using Windows
on your local machine,

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.430
install a third party RDP
client such as Chrome RDP

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:01.220
by Fusion Labs.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.920
One more thing that I personally
love about Google Compute

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:05.420
Engine is that
our infrastructure

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.180
is entirely carbon neutral.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:09.710
Our global network
of data centers

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:13.220
consume 50% less energy than
the typical data center.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:15.410
And we purchase enough
renewable energy

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:18.230
to match 100% of
the energy consumed

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:20.210
by our global operations.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:22.470
We are growing our global
data center footprint

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:25.430
so your applications can
run closer to your customers

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:27.950
and distribute geographically
for resiliency.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.000
I think that's pretty cool.

